  "overview": "**One UI** is a light-first design system anchored on `#fff` canvas surfaces with `#0b0b0c` primary ink (19.7:1 contrast) and `#007bff` brand accent.\n\nDisplay headlines pair `Samsung SS Head` with `System UI` body copy (96px display down to 16px body), unified by `0.25rem` base corner radius and subtle shadow elevation.\n\nMaintained by **Samsung**. Source: live stylesheet extraction (https://developer.samsung.com/one-ui). Inventory: **24** colors, **23** typography steps, and **78** documented components (all rights reserved license).\n\n### Layout & Spacing\n- **Grid & Control Spacing**: Derived from 78 component tokens with documented paddings: `.5rem`, `0`, `1.4375rem`, `100px 120px`, `0 16px`.\n- **Hierarchy**: Group controls cleanly within `#f8f9fa` cards; separate sibling sections using `color-mix(in srgb, #0b0b0c 14%, transparent)` hairlines rather than oversized whitespace.\n\n### Elevation & Depth\n- **Layered Shadow Model**: Uses documented shadows (`0 10px 40px rgba(5,40,50,.1)`, `0 0.25rem 0.75rem rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1)`) paired with `color-mix(in srgb, #0b0b0c 14%, transparent)` borders for elevated overlays.\n- **Interactive Lift**: Reserve higher surface brightness or focus outlines anchored on `#007bff` for keyboard focus and active selection states.",
  "dos": "### Do\n- Anchor base views on `#fff` (light) with `#0b0b0c` primary text and `#0b0b0c` secondary labels.\n- Use `#007bff` with `#f7f7f8` text (3.7:1) for primary CTAs, active tabs, and focus outlines.\n- Pair `Samsung SS Head` headings with `System UI` body copy using documented weights and scale steps.\n- Apply `0.25rem` base geometry across inputs and buttons (.875rem on outer containers).\n- Separate containers via `#f8f9fa` surface shifts and `color-mix(in srgb, #0b0b0c 14%, transparent)` hairlines cleanly.\n\n### Don't\n- Do not invert the base canvas out of light polarity without explicitly switching component text tokens.\n- Do not place low-contrast muted ink or raw white text on light accents without verifying >= 4.5:1 WCAG AA contrast.\n- Do not invent arbitrary brand colors, unverified fonts, or synthetic heavy shadows outside the palette above.\n- Do not mix conflicting corner radii that clash with the system's `0.25rem` baseline.\n- Do not truncate or drop border contrast on `accordion-list-v3-search-box` fields and secondary buttons."
